Check out the PR head. Run every check below at that head, in order, and report PASS or FAIL for each with the evidence (commands and output).

Setup: at the repo root run npm ci. Create temp files in a scratch dir outside the repo, e.g.:
- clean.jsonl: {"a":1}\n[2]\n"x"\n
- badmid.jsonl: {"a":1}\n{bad\n{"c":3}\n
- torn.jsonl: {"a":1}\n{"b":2}\n{"c": (no trailing newline)
- blanks.jsonl: {"a":1}\n\n   \n{oops\n\n (row 4 bad; rows 2, 3, 5 blank)

Check 1 — expect: "packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js <file> prints <file>:<line>: <error> for every row that is not valid JSON (1-based lines, blank lines skipped, an unterminated last line checked) and exits 1 if any, 0 if none".
Run node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js <path> for each temp file and record stdout and exit status.
PASS if: clean.jsonl prints no error lines and exits 0; badmid.jsonl prints a line starting with <path>:2: followed by an error text, no line for rows 1 or 3, and exits 1; torn.jsonl prints a line starting with <path>:3: and exits 1; blanks.jsonl prints a line starting with <path>:4: , no lines for blank rows 2, 3 or 5, and exits 1. Also try a file with two bad rows and confirm both are printed.
FAIL if any of those outputs or exit statuses differ (wrong line number, missing row, blank row reported, torn last row ignored, wrong exit code).

Check 2 — expect: "A missing file or no argument prints to stderr and exits 2".
Run node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js /nonexistent/x.jsonl, and node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js with no argument, capturing stderr and exit status separately.
PASS if both exit 2 and both write something non-empty to stderr.
FAIL if either exits with any other status or writes nothing to stderr.

Check 3 — expect: "packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js exports lint(text) returning [{ line, error }]".
Run: node --input-type=module -e "import {lint} from './packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js'; console.log(JSON.stringify(lint('{}\n{bad\n')), JSON.stringify(lint('{}\n')))" at the repo root.
PASS if lint is an exported function, the first call returns an array of objects each having a line property (2 for the bad row) and an error property, and the clean call returns an empty array.
FAIL if the import fails, lint is not exported, or the return shape is not an array of { line, error } objects.

Check 4 — expect: "The workspace has its own package.json (jsonl-lint, type module, test script node --test), no runtime dependencies, and node:test tests for a clean file, a bad middle row, a torn last row, blank lines and the exit codes".
Read packages/jsonl-lint/package.json and run cd packages/jsonl-lint && npm test. Read the test files.
PASS if package.json has name jsonl-lint, type module, a test script that runs node --test, no non-empty dependencies field; npm test passes; and the tests (using node:test) cover a clean file, a bad middle row, a torn last row, blank lines, and the CLI exit codes.
FAIL if any field is wrong or missing, there are runtime dependencies, tests fail, or any of the five listed cases has no test.

Check 5 — expect: "packages/jsonl-lint/README.md exists and the root README lists the tool".
Run test -f packages/jsonl-lint/README.md and grep -n jsonl-lint README.md.
PASS if the package README exists and the root README.md mentions jsonl-lint as a tool.
FAIL if either is missing.

Check 6 — expect: "The change is one PR on suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test whose body says Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102, and npm test and the test workflow are green at its head".
